{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short; git rev-parse HEAD; git log --oneline --decorate -8; git show cfd3b9cbbf464c045f1ff37b1a6da040a229a7d9:attest/specs/204.md 2>/dev/null || git show cfd3b9cbbf464c045f1ff37b1a6da040a229a7d9:attest/specs/204/spec.md 2>/dev/null || find attest/specs/204 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print; git diff cfd3b9cbbf464c045f1ff37b1a6da040a229a7d9 b862f4f30f432b56a72b6475f664f885d95a1af6 -- tests/test_attest_time.py attavo/doctor.py; rg -n \"type Item(Time|Cost)|ItemTime|ItemCost|by_stage_usd|attestation.schema\" attavo/types.py schema/attestation.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-tRwRgrsC' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-gN24vKhQ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Yf6Dw7aV' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-RDxzULMx' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n5ac0174b0d4173f87a427c0de686a633d4df3be0\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-9mv1UDZa' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-mugQdnVG' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n5ac0174 (HEAD -> attavo/204-proof-six-whole, origin/attavo/204-proof-six-whole) attavo: verify invocation 01 started for item 204\n885dca5 attavo: build record for item 204 (build-01)\nb862f4f proof six holds a sealed statement to its whole accounting, exactly (#202, #203)\nf55ce0c attavo: build invocation 01 started for item 204\n6d14eb6 attavo: approval record for item 204\ne5cfa1c attavo: spec-gate record for item 204\ncfd3b9c spec for #204: proof six holds a sealed statement to its whole accounting, exactly\n9b3e2c7 (origin/main, origin/gh-readonly-queue/main/pr-195-950812aba18b4f1766815671103a733f75e71de4, origin/HEAD, main) Merge pull request #195 from attavo/attavo/194-statement-time\n## Problem\n\nProof six holds each sealed statement to its records, and the release that adds the statement's `time` and `cost` (#194) checks one number of them loosely. The review of #194 filed both halves. #202: `_time_disagrees` allows `abs(stated - summed) <= 1.0`, so a statement saying 398.75 of records that sum to 398.25 holds, although both sides are the same function's rounding of the same records and cannot honestly differ at all. #203: only `time.invocation_s` is compared, so the per-stage seconds and attempts, `lead_s`, `waiting_s`, `partial`, `not_read`, and every field of `cost` can say anything while the proof holds. No sealed statement carries `time` yet (the pinned release prints none), so this lands before the first one that does and wedges nothing that exists.\n\nThe check this replaces also excepted nothing on purpose but could not have checked `lead_s`: it passed no seal time. The statement is computed at the merge commit (read on #194's own sealed statement: its `sha` is the merge on `main`), so the doctor recomputes `lead_s` and `waiting_s` from that commit's committer time and excepts no field.\n\nTwo rules keep a sealed, immutable statement from ever wedging the doctor, the lesson of #194's `verify-01`: numbers are compared as numbers (a store may print 40.0 as 40), and only the keys a statement carries are compared, so a field a later release adds is not demanded of a statement sealed before it. A key the statement carries that the function does not produce is a disagreement, as is one of `time` and `cost` without the other.\n\nRetires: `_time_disagrees` and its one-second tolerance; the comparison of one field standing for the accounting; #202; #203.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/doctor.py\n- attavo/attest.py\n- tests/test_attest_time.py\n- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- doctor-fails-a-subsecond-disagreement.sh: on a fixture item whose records sum to 398.25, proof every-attested-item-is-sealed fails a sealed statement whose time.invocation_s says 398.75, naming item 1 and time.invocation_s\n- doctor-fails-every-field-that-is-not-its-records.sh: the proof holds on the statement attest printed, and on the same statement with 40.0 printed as 40 and one key absent; it fails, naming item 1 and the field, when any of time.build.invocation_s, time.lead_s, time.waiting_s, time.not_read, cost.usd, cost.by_adapter_usd, cost.partial, or cost.not_read is not what the records sum to while time.invocation_s stays true, when the statement carries a cost key the function does not produce, and when it carries time without cost; it does not check a statement that carries neither\n- the-whole-accounting-has-its-tests.sh: tests/test_attest_time.py carries the three tests by name, attavo/doctor.py has no _time_disagrees and no tolerance, and calls item_time_and_cost exactly once\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Oflg36OL' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-LQdQw8os' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ndiff --git a/attavo/doctor.py b/attavo/doctor.py\nindex c6e2d15..71cd3bf 100644\n--- a/attavo/doctor.py\n+++ b/attavo/doctor.py\n@@ -631,23 +631,72 @@ def _is_ancestor(root: Path, earlier: str, later: str) -> bool:\n     return run.returncode == 0\n \n \n-def _time_disagrees(item_records_dir: Path, item: str, merge_sha: str,\n-                    statement: dict[str, Any]) -> str | None:\n-    \"\"\"A sealed statement that carries `time` says the invocation_s its\n-    records sum to -- the same function attest summed them with, over the\n-    same records (no record is written after a merge). A statement sealed\n-    before `time` existed carries none and is not checked. No new read of\n-    the store: the statement is the one proof six already holds.\"\"\"\n+# Maps whose keys are the records' data (a stage or an adapter that cost\n+# something), not a release's fields: a key missing from one is a difference.\n+DATA_KEYED = (\"by_stage_usd\", \"by_adapter_usd\")\n+\n+\n+def _same(stated: Any, summed: Any) -> bool:\n+    \"\"\"Equal as the accounting means it: a number equals a number of the\n+    same value (a store may print 40.0 as 40), a bool equals only a bool,\n+    and a list is equal member by member. No tolerance: both sides are the\n+    same function's rounding of the same records.\"\"\"\n+    if isinstance(stated, bool) or isinstance(summed, bool):\n+        return isinstance(stated, bool) and isinstance(summed, bool) and stated == summed\n+    if isinstance(stated, (int, float)) and isinstance(summed, (int, float)):\n+        return float(stated) == float(summed)\n+    if isinstance(stated, list) and isinstance(summed, list):\n+        return len(stated) == len(summed) and all(_same(a, b) for a, b in zip(stated, summed))\n+    return type(stated) is type(summed) and bool(stated == summed)\n+\n+\n+def _differences(path: str, stated: Any, summed: Any, keyed_by_data: bool = False) -> list[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Every field of `stated` that is not what its records sum to, named by\n+    its path. Only the keys the statement carries are compared, at every\n+    depth, so a field a later release adds is not demanded of a statement\n+    sealed before it; a key it carries that the function does not produce\n+    is a difference.\"\"\"\n+    if not (isinstance(stated, dict) and isinstance(summed, dict)):\n+        return [] if _same(stated, summed) else [f\"{path} {stated!r} is not its records' {summed!r}\"]\n+    found: list[str] = []\n+    for key in sorted(stated):\n+        if key not in summed:\n+            found.append(f\"{path}.{key} {stated[key]!r} is not a field its records sum to\")\n+        else:\n+            found += _differences(f\"{path}.{key}\", stated[key], summed[key], key in DATA_KEYED)\n+    if keyed_by_data:\n+        found += [f\"{path}.{key} is absent; its records sum to {summed[key]!r}\"\n+                  for key in sorted(summed.keys() - stated.keys())]\n+    return found\n+\n+\n+def _accounting_disagrees(root: Path, item_records_dir: Path, item: str, merge_sha: str,\n+                          statement: dict[str, Any]) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"A sealed statement that carries `time` and `cost` says what its\n+    records sum to, field by field -- the same function attest summed them\n+    with, over the same records (none is written after a merge), sealed at\n+    the same commit (the statement is computed at the merge, so lead_s and\n+    waiting_s are recomputed from its committer time, not excepted). Exact:\n+    #202 retired the one-second tolerance. A statement sealed before `time`\n+    existed carries neither block and is not checked; one block without the\n+    other is a disagreement. No new read of the store.\"\"\"\n     inner = statement.get(\"predicate\")\n     predicate = inner if isinstance(inner, dict) else statement\n-    stated_time = predicate.get(\"time\")\n-    if not isinstance(stated_time, dict):\n+    stated_time, stated_cost = predicate.get(\"time\"), predicate.get(\"cost\")\n+    if stated_time is None and stated_cost is None:\n         return None\n-    summed = item_time_and_cost(item_records_dir, None)[0][\"invocation_s\"]\n-    stated = stated_time.get(\"invocation_s\")\n-    if isinstance(stated, bool) or not isinstance(stated, (int, float)) or abs(stated - summed) > 1.0:\n-        return (f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}: the statement's time.invocation_s \"\n-                f\"{stated} is not its records' {summed}\")\n+    where = f\"item {item} merged at {merge_sha[:12]}\"\n+    if not isinstance(stated_time, dict) or not isinstance(stated_cost, dict):\n+        return f\"{where}: the statement carries one of time and cost without the other\"\n+    try:\n+        sealed_at: int | None = int(git(root, \"show\", \"-s\", \"--format=%ct\", merge_sha).strip())\n+    except (RuntimeError, ValueError):\n+        sealed_at = None\n+    summed_time, summed_cost = item_time_and_cost(item_records_dir, sealed_at)\n+    differing = (_differences(\"time\", stated_time, dict(summed_time))\n+                 + _differences(\"cost\", stated_cost, dict(summed_cost)))\n+    if differing:\n+        return f\"{where}: the statement's \" + \"; \".join(differing)\n     return None\n \n \n@@ -696,7 +745,8 @@ def proof_every_attested_item_is_sealed(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) ->\n         statement, exit_code = statement_for(root, cmd, merge_sha)\n         if statement is not None:\n             sealed.append(item)\n-            disagreement = _time_disagrees(records_dir / item, item, merge_sha, statement)\n+            disagreement = _accounting_disagrees(root, records_dir / item, item, merge_sha,\n+                                                 statement)\n             if disagreement:\n                 reasons.append(disagreement)\n         elif exit_code == 2:\ndiff --git a/tests/test_attest_time.py b/tests/test_attest_time.py\nindex b4eda86..08fef01 100644\n--- a/tests/test_attest_time.py\n+++ b/tests/test_attest_time.py\n@@ -162,7 +162,87 @@ def test_doctor_proof_six_fails_a_statement_whose_time_is_not_its_records(tmp_pa\n     assert failed[\"holds\"] is False, failed\n     assert \"item 1\" in failed[\"reason\"] and \"time.invocation_s\" in failed[\"reason\"], failed\n \n-    # a statement sealed before `time` existed carries none and is not checked\n+    # a statement sealed before `time` and `cost` existed carries neither\n+    # and is not checked; one without the other is a disagreement (#203)\n     del statement[\"time\"]\n+    del statement[\"cost\"]\n     (store / f\"{merge}.json\").write_text(json.dumps(envelope))\n     assert proof_six(root)[\"holds\"] is True\n+\n+\n+def seal(root: Path, merge: str, statement: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n+    store = root / \"statements\"\n+    store.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n+    envelope = {\"_type\": \"https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\", \"predicate\": statement}\n+    (store / f\"{merge}.json\").write_text(json.dumps(envelope))\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_rejects_a_subsecond_time_invocation_mismatch(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"#202: the check allowed one second either way, so a statement could\n+    say 398.75 of records that sum to 398.25 and hold.\"\"\"\n+    root, merge = make_item(tmp_path, INVOCATIONS)\n+    statement = attest(root)\n+    assert statement[\"time\"][\"invocation_s\"] == 398.25\n+    statement[\"time\"][\"invocation_s\"] = 398.75\n+    seal(root, merge, statement)\n+    failed = proof_six(root)\n+    assert failed[\"holds\"] is False, failed\n+    assert \"item 1\" in failed[\"reason\"] and \"time.invocation_s\" in failed[\"reason\"], failed\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_rejects_statement_whose_time_or_cost_breakdown_disagrees_with_records(\n+        tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"#203: only time.invocation_s was compared, so every other field of\n+    the accounting could say anything. Each case leaves invocation_s true.\"\"\"\n+    root, merge = make_item(tmp_path, INVOCATIONS)\n+    true_statement = attest(root)\n+    seal(root, merge, true_statement)\n+    assert proof_six(root)[\"holds\"] is True\n+\n+    def forged(path: tuple[str, ...], value: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+        copy: dict[str, Any] = json.loads(json.dumps(true_statement))\n+        node = copy\n+        for key in path[:-1]:\n+            node = node[key]\n+        node[path[-1]] = value\n+        return copy\n+\n+    cases: list[tuple[tuple[str, ...], Any, str]] = [\n+        ((\"time\", \"build\", \"invocation_s\"), 1.0, \"time.build\"),\n+        ((\"time\", \"build\", \"attempts\"), 1, \"time.build\"),\n+        ((\"time\", \"lead_s\"), 1.0, \"time.lead_s\"),\n+        ((\"time\", \"waiting_s\"), 1.0, \"time.waiting_s\"),\n+        ((\"time\", \"partial\"), True, \"time.partial\"),\n+        ((\"time\", \"not_read\"), [\"build-02\"], \"time.not_read\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"usd\"), 0.5, \"cost.usd\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"by_stage_usd\"), {\"build\": 0.5}, \"cost.by_stage_usd\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"by_adapter_usd\"), {\"alpha\": 0.5}, \"cost.by_adapter_usd\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"partial\"), False, \"cost.partial\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"not_read\"), [], \"cost.not_read\"),\n+        ((\"cost\", \"rate_usd\"), 1.0, \"cost.rate_usd\"),\n+    ]\n+    for path, value, named in cases:\n+        seal(root, merge, forged(path, value))\n+        failed = proof_six(root)\n+        assert failed[\"holds\"] is False, (path, failed)\n+        assert \"item 1\" in failed[\"reason\"] and named in failed[\"reason\"], (path, failed)\n+\n+    one_block: dict[str, Any] = json.loads(json.dumps(true_statement))\n+    del one_block[\"cost\"]\n+    seal(root, merge, one_block)\n+    assert proof_six(root)[\"holds\"] is False\n+\n+\n+def test_doctor_holds_a_true_statement_however_its_store_prints_it(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"The rule that keeps a sealed statement from wedging the doctor: a\n+    store may print 40.0 as 40, and a release after the seal may add a\n+    field the sealed statement never carried. Neither is a disagreement.\"\"\"\n+    root, merge = make_item(tmp_path, INVOCATIONS)\n+    statement = attest(root)\n+    assert statement[\"time\"][\"verify\"][\"invocation_s\"] == 40.0\n+    statement[\"time\"][\"verify\"][\"invocation_s\"] = 40\n+    del statement[\"time\"][\"counsel\"]\n+    del statement[\"time\"][\"build\"][\"partial\"]\n+    seal(root, merge, statement)\n+    held = proof_six(root)\n+    assert held[\"holds\"] is True and held[\"sealed\"] == [\"1\"], held\nschema/attestation.schema.json:10:    \"tokens_by_stage\", \"cost_by_stage_usd\", \"wall_clock_by_stage_s\", \"time\", \"cost\",\nschema/attestation.schema.json:63:    \"cost_by_stage_usd\": {\nschema/attestation.schema.json:102:      \"required\": [\"usd\", \"by_stage_usd\", \"by_adapter_usd\", \"partial\", \"not_read\"],\nschema/attestation.schema.json:105:        \"by_stage_usd\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0}},\nattavo/types.py:152:class ItemTime(TypedDict):\nattavo/types.py:166:class ItemCost(TypedDict):\nattavo/types.py:172:    by_stage_usd: dict[str, float]\nattavo/types.py:179:    \"\"\"The statement `attavo attest` prints (schema/attestation.schema.json).\"\"\"\nattavo/types.py:195:    cost_by_stage_usd: dict[str, float | None]\nattavo/types.py:197:    time: ItemTime\nattavo/types.py:198:    cost: ItemCost\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
